        "answer": {
          "short": "$P(A\\cap B)=\\frac{2}{3}a$, $P(B)=\\frac{4}{3}a$.",
          "worked": "Using $P(B\\mid A)=\\dfrac{P(A\\cap B)}{P(A)}$,\n$$\\begin{align*}P(A\\cap B)&=P(B\\mid A)P(A)\\\\P(A\\cap B)&=\\frac{2}{3}a.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $P(A\\mid B)=\\dfrac{P(A\\cap B)}{P(B)}$,\n$$\\begin{align*}P(B)&=\\frac{P(A\\cap B)}{P(A\\mid B)}\\\\P(B)&=\\frac{\\frac{2}{3}a}{\\frac{1}{2}}\\\\P(B)&=\\frac{4}{3}a.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 68
      },
