        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=\\frac{9}{20}$.\n\nSubstitute the expressions from part (a) into the addition rule.",
          "worked": "By the addition rule,\n$$\\begin{align*}P(A\\cup B)&=P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B)\\\\\\frac{3}{4}&=a+\\frac{4}{3}a-\\frac{2}{3}a\\\\\\frac{3}{4}&=\\frac{5}{3}a\\\\a&=\\frac{3}{4}\\times\\frac{3}{5}\\\\a&=\\frac{9}{20}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
