        "answer": {
          "short": "Not independent.\n\nCompare $P(A\\cap B)=\\frac{3}{10}$ with $P(A)P(B)=\\frac{27}{100}$; they are unequal.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(A\\cap B)&=\\frac{2}{3}\\times\\frac{9}{20}\\\\P(A\\cap B)&=\\frac{3}{10}\\\\P(B)&=\\frac{4}{3}\\times\\frac{9}{20}\\\\P(B)&=\\frac{3}{5}\\\\P(A)P(B)&=\\frac{9}{20}\\times\\frac{3}{5}\\\\P(A)P(B)&=\\frac{27}{100}.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $P(A\\cap B)\\ne P(A)P(B)$, $A$ and $B$ are not independent.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
